PROJECT DETAILS :

1.	Project Title
Attendance Tracking System using Python

2.	Problem Statement
To design and develop a Python program that manages and tracks student attendance efficiently. The system should allow adding students, marking attendance, calculating attendance percentage, and displaying attendance reports.

3.	Objective
The objective of this project is to create a simple attendance management system using Python that stores attendance records and calculates attendance percentage using loops, functions, and conditional statements.


4.	Tools Used
Python IDLE / Python Compiler


5.	Description
•	This project is used to maintain student attendance digitally.
•	The user can add student names.
•	The user can mark attendance as Present (P) or Absent (A).
•	The program stores attendance records.
•	The system calculates attendance percentage.
•	The program displays attendance report.

6.	Algorithm
1.	Start
2.	Create an empty dictionary to store students
3.	Display menu options
4.	Add Student
5.	Mark Attendance
6.	View Attendance
7.	Calculate Percentage
8.	Exit
9.	Read user choice
10.	If choice = Add Student → Add name to dictionary
11.	If choice = Mark Attendance → Store P/A status
12.	If choice = View Attendance → Display attendance list
13.	If choice = Calculate Percentage → Compute percentage
14.	If choice = Exit → Stop program
15.	Stop

7.	Program (Python Code)

print("------ Attendance Tracking System	")
students = {}
while True:
print("\n1. Add Student") print("2. Mark Attendance") print("3. View Attendance") print("4. Calculate Percentage") print("5. Exit")
choice = input("Enter your choice: ")
if choice == "1":
name = input("Enter student name: ")
 
students[name] = []
print("Student added successfully!")
elif choice == "2":
name = input("Enter student name: ") if name in students:
status = input("Enter status (P/A): ").upper() students[name].append(status) print("Attendance marked!")
else:
print("Student not found!")
elif choice == "3":
name = input("Enter student name: ") if name in students:
print("Attendance Record:", students[name]) else:
print("Student not found!")
elif choice == "4":
name = input("Enter student name: ") if name in students:
total = len(students[name])
present = students[name].count("P") if total == 0:
print("No attendance records available.") else:
percentage = (present / total) * 100 print("Attendance Percentage:", percentage, "%")
else:
print("Student not found!")
elif choice == "5": print("Exiting program...") break
else:
print("Invalid choice!")


9.Result
The Attendance Tracking System successfully manages student attendance records and calculates attendance percentage using Python programming concepts.

10.Conclusion
This project demonstrates how Python can be used to manage and track attendance efficiently. It improves understanding of dictionaries, loops, conditional statements, and functions in Python.

 
